{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1254912-a-few-questions-about-the-old-mythologies-book","id":1254912,"title":"A few questions about the old Mythologies book","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-16T21:11:25-07:00","id":1254912,"title":"A few questions about the old Mythologies book","content":"So people, does anyone still use that book? How up to date is it or not? Are the concepts there still raw/fresh or have some (or all) of the ideas in that book been superseded by later and more fleshed out stuff in later works?<br /> <br /> It has been quite some time since i last tinkered with setting-building (probably a little before Strix Chronicles, goddamn) and wished to get some input from other people on the book and related stuff, to have some fun tweaking/updating materials of that book, but also to avoid the pitfall of reinventing already existing wheels without meaning to where possible.<br /> <br /> - I know for a fact Bloody Mary (described in Mythologies as one of two patrons of Ars Speculorum) got considerable expansion in Danse Macabre at least, with a shadow cult/sub-covenant (and possible tie-ins to the Hedge). A Hollow Mekhet's wandering Ka also play with Mirrors, so another association/connection through that might be possible too.<br /> <br /> - I <i>think </i>something like the Imago might have appeared in Danse Macabre too, if memory tricks me not (and it might, <i>really </i>have to check that up).<br /> <br /> - Sin-Eaters, Breath Drinkers and Blood Curses, maybe, but i'm far from sure.<br /> <br /> - The Blood Gods systems should be quite adaptable into Shadow Cult Initiations and Elder disciplines with some polishing and boost, i guess.<br /> <br /> So, anyways, any input or book references - Requiem or not - are more than welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-17-2018, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T22:09:15-07:00","id":1254921,"title":"","content":"The Solace drug is first mentioned in Mythologies, and it gets a sidebar in the Second Edition core. It's also obliquely referred to in Kiss of the Succubus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"than